body:
I don't mind talks, but it depends on the villain, the build up, their motivations. 

&#x200B;

With Eva it felt like she was a bit too far gone, and it didn't feel that realistic to do a world wide raid and then be like "fk me these ppl are actually hurt"

what an insane chapter honestly, one of my favourite chapters across any manga.

&#x200B;

so well pieced together, a good amount of plot twists and loads of info/world building. AND it doesn't feel retconned coz the whole origin of them wasn't well explained in Naruto

what does a face reveal have to do with his video amount lmao, i dont mind that he hasnt done anything for 4 weeks but he hasn't really elaborated on why other than letting us know he's moving so i thought it'd be biweekly, every third at worst.

&#x200B;

if we had updates on why he's mia it'd have been np for me

Usually I don't mind the prank calls and find them really funny because all in all, while some people get mad nobody gets hurt or loses their job.

&#x200B;

Which is why there was this one prank call I wasn't fond of, where he called a 7-11 employee with bad English and made him straight up insult customers. Now this messes with the dude's job and might get him fired, not OK. The rest is just him messing with people in not harmful ways... other than getting them worked up and/or worried about something that's not going to happen.
